@startuml SAYCEP_A3_Deployment
' Assignment 3 Q3.6 - deployment diagram: the demonstration environment.
title SAYCEP - Deployment Diagram (demonstration environment)
skinparam shadowing false

node "Presenter laptop - Windows 11, Python 3.10+" as Laptop {
  node "uvicorn process, port 8000" as Proc {
    artifact "backend/*.py" as Code
    artifact "frontend/ static files" as Static
  }
  database "saycep.db\nSQLite file, 8.2 MB" as DB
  folder "backend/data/onet/\n41 text files, 97 MB" as Onet
}

node "Web browser - Chrome, Edge or Firefox" as Browser {
  artifact "index.html + app.js\nReact vendored locally" as Page
}

cloud "Internet - not required at runtime" as Net {
  node "Google Fonts" as Fonts
  node "cdnjs / jsDelivr\nfallback only" as CDN
}
cloud "Kaggle" as Kaggle

Browser --> Proc : HTTP localhost:8000
Proc --> DB : sqlite3, one connection per request
Onet --> DB : load_onet.py, manual rebuild in 0.6 s
Kaggle ..> Onet : one-time download, login required
Browser ..> Fonts : optional, system fonts otherwise
Browser ..> CDN : only if a vendored file is missing

note bottom of Laptop
  Single machine. Browser and server can be the same laptop.
  Production target in the proposal: containerised API behind
  a load balancer, dataset read-only and replicated.
end note
@enduml
